ven-names></name><name><surname>Magdelenat</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Real-time quantitative PCR determination of urokinase-type plasminogen activator receptor (uPAR) expression of isolated micrometastatic cells from bone marrow of breast cancer patients.</article-title> <source>Int J Cancer</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>114</volume>:<fpage>291</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15543615</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferrucci</surname><given-names>PF</given-names></name><name><surname>Rabascio</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gigli</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>A new comprehensive gene expression panel to study tumor micrometastasis in patients with high-risk breast cancer.</article-title> <source>Int J Oncol</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>30</volume>:<fpage>955</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17332935</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vincent-Salomon</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pierga</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></name><name><surname>Couturier</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>HER2 status of bone marrow micrometastasis and their corresponding primary tumours in a pilot study of 27 cases: a possible tool for anti-HER2 therapy management?</article-title> <source>Br J Cancer</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>96</volume>:<fpage>654</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17262082</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Slade</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Coombes</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>The clinical significance of disseminated tumor cells in breast cancer.</article-title> <source>Nat Clin Pract Oncol</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>4</volume>:<fpage>30</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17183354</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gerber</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Krause</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Simultaneous immunohistochemical detection of tumor cells in lymph nodes and bone marrow aspirates in breast cancer and its correlation with other prognostic factors.</article-title> <source>J Clin Oncol</source> <year>2001</year>;<volume>19</volume>:<fpage>960</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11181658</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gebauer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Fehm</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Merkle</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Epithelial cells in bone marrow of breast cancer patients at time of primary surgery: clinical outcome during long-term follow-up.</article-title> <source>J Clin Oncol</source> <year>2001</year>;<volume>19</volume>:<fpage>3669</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11504748</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Braun</surname><given-names>S</given-